(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #157: two values holding texts compare by their
 characters, in a condition and as a value, at the top level and in a
 function.)

a value called word is "ab".
a value called 'same word' is "{word}".
a value called 'other word' is "ba".
a value called count is 5.
a value called 'number text' is "5".
If word is 'same word' then, Print "word is same word".
Otherwise, Print "word is not same word"..
If word is not 'other word' then, Print "word is not other word".
Otherwise, Print "word is other word"..
If count is 'number text' then, Print "a number is a text".
Otherwise, Print "a number is not a text"..
a boolean called 'they match' is word is 'same word'.
Print "{they match}".

To 'compare the words' with a value called left and a value called right.
    If left is right then, Print "{left} and {right} are the same".
    Otherwise, Print "{left} and {right} differ"..

'compare the words' with word and 'same word'.
'compare the words' with word and 'other word'.

a list called pair is ["cd", "{word}"].
For each item in pair,
    If item is word then, Print "{item} matches word".
    Otherwise, Print "{item} does not match word"..
